# Git Conventions

## Branch Naming

```
feat/sd-187-rename-roles-to-plans   # Feature from Jira ticket
fix/timer-not-stopping               # Bug fix
chore/update-dependencies            # Maintenance
```

## Commit Messages

Format: `type(scope): description (SD-xxx)`

```
feat(stride-types): add TaskPriority and BreakType enums (SD-80)

Add 9 new enums required by the Figma UI design.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
```

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `refactor`, `test`, `docs`
Scopes: `stride-types`, `stride-db`, `stride-core`, `stride-desktop`, `stride-ui`

## What to Commit

- Source code changes
- Test files
- Config changes (tsconfig, package.json, vite.config)

## What NOT to Commit

- `node_modules/`, `dist/`, `.env*` (except `.env.example`)
- Secrets, API keys, credentials
- Large binary files

## Build Verification

Before considering any task complete, run builds and tests for all affected packages:

```bash
# stride-types
cd stride-types && yarn build

# stride-db (depends on stride-types)
cd stride-db && yarn build && yarn test

# stride-core (depends on stride-db)
cd stride-core && yarn build && yarn test

# stride-desktop (depends on stride-core)
cd stride-desktop && yarn build
```

If you changed `@stridetime/types`, rebuild everything downstream in order:
`types → db → core → desktop`
